    <div class="hbadge rv in">Journal · Guide</div>
    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">How Do You Plan a Day Around a Morning Boat Trip in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>15 November 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">Take the 10:00 Day Trip, step back onto the pontoon at 12:30 or 13:00, eat lunch in Funchal, then drive west to Câmara de Lobos and the Cabo Girão skywalk and end the day at Ponta do Sol for sunset. You see the same cliffs from the sea in the morning and from 580 metres up in the afternoon.</p>

      <h2>Why does a morning boat make the rest of the day easy?</h2><p>Because it is over by lunch. The part of the day that depends most on the sea is done early, and the afternoon on land works whatever the forecast does next.</p><p>It also gives the day a shape. In the morning you pass under Cabo Girão and look up. In the afternoon you stand on top and look down at the water you crossed. Few days on the island join up as neatly.</p><h2>The plan, hour by hour</h2><h3>09:45: be on the pontoon</h3><p>Be on the pontoon at Marina do Funchal by 09:45, a quarter of an hour before the boat leaves, and the skipper will be there to meet you. Eat a light breakfast, put on sun cream at the hotel and wear swimwear under your clothes.</p><h3>10:00 to 12:30 or 13:00: the coast from the sea</h3><p>The Chifbay <a href="/hidden-coves-half-day">Day Trip along the south coast</a> shows you this afternoon's places from below first: Câmara de Lobos from the water, then Cabo Girão from its foot, with the drone up overhead if the weather allows. The swims come after, at Fajã dos Padres, where the paddle boards come out too, and at Ribeira Brava, before a quick run home. Choose the 3h trip, back at 13:00, and you also reach Ponta do Sol, the same village where you will watch tonight's sunset.</p><p>Look up at the top of Cabo Girão as you pass beneath it. The platform you can just make out at the top is where you will stand in the afternoon.</p><h3>13:00 to 14:30: lunch in Funchal</h3><p>Walk from the marina into the centre or the old town. For speed, order a prego no bolo do caco: steak in a garlic flatbread. An espetada takes longer and is worth it if you have the time. If your hotel is close, go back for a shower first, because salt water dries sticky. Arrange the hire car for about 14:30.</p><h3>14:45: drive to Câmara de Lobos</h3><p>Câmara de Lobos is about 15 minutes west of Funchal by car, more in traffic. Park above the town and walk down to the harbour, where brightly painted fishing boats sit pulled up by the water. The bay is the one Winston Churchill painted during his stay in January 1950, and a viewpoint at the entrance to the town now carries his name.</p><p>This is also the town most linked with poncha. If you want a glass, let the passengers have it: the driver has a cliff road ahead. Our <a href="/posts/camara-de-lobos-madeira-guide">Câmara de Lobos guide</a> covers the town in more depth.</p><h3>16:00: the Cabo Girão skywalk</h3><p>Drive on and uphill to Cabo Girão. The glass platform sits about 580 metres above the sea, and from it you look straight down on the small terraced fields at the foot of the cliff and on the water you crossed in the morning. In 2026 entry costs 5 EUR for visitors and is free for children up to 12 and for Madeira residents. It is open in daylight, with shorter hours in winter, so check before you go.</p><p>If heights make you feel ill, it depends how badly. You can stand back from the glass and still take in the view, or skip the platform and keep the morning's picture of the cliff from below. We compared the two in <a href="/posts/cabo-girao-from-the-sea">Cabo Girão from the sea</a>.</p><h3>17:00 to sunset: west to Ponta do Sol</h3><p>From Cabo Girão, Ponta do Sol is about 20 minutes west by car. The small town sits on the sea between steep hills, and its seafront is one of the classic places on the south coast to watch the evening. In winter you drive straight there. In summer you have time for a swim at the beach and a slow dinner before the light goes.</p><h2>How does the plan change with the season?</h2><p>The morning stays the same all year. The afternoon stretches or shrinks with the sunset.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Season</th><th>Sunset in Funchal, roughly</th><th>What to change</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>December and January</td><td>About 18:00 to 18:30</td><td>Short afternoon. Skip the shower stop and go from lunch straight to the car.</td></tr><tr><td>Spring and autumn</td><td>Somewhere in between</td><td>Check the sunset time for your date and follow the plan as written.</td></tr><tr><td>June and July</td><td>About 21:15</td><td>Long afternoon. Add a swim at Ponta do Sol or a slower lunch.</td></tr></tbody></table><p>In December, the Cabo Girão stop and the drive to Ponta do Sol use most of the light you have, so do not linger in Câmara de Lobos. In June, the long evening lets you add the beach at Ponta do Sol without rushing anything.</p><h2>When is this plan too much for one day?</h2><p>It depends on your group. The plan is two big outdoor blocks: sea and sun in the morning, cliffs and driving in the afternoon. It is too much if:</p><ul><li>someone in the group gets seasick and needs the afternoon to recover;</li><li>you have small children who nap after lunch;</li><li>nobody wants to drive, since taxis work but make the day slower and dearer;</li><li>you arrived by cruise ship and must be back on board in the afternoon. Then the boat is your day.</li></ul><p>In those cases, split it. Do the boat one day and Câmara de Lobos with Cabo Girão the next. Or swap the morning trip for an evening one: our comparison of the <a href="/posts/day-trip-vs-sunset-cruise-madeira">Day Trip and the Sunset Trip</a> helps you choose.</p><h2>What do you need for the day?</h2><ul><li>Swimwear, a towel and a dry change of clothes for after the boat.</li><li>Sun cream, a hat and sunglasses. The sun on the water and on the skywalk is strong for most of the year.</li><li>A hire car booked for the afternoon, with someone happy to drive cliff roads.</li><li>Cash or a card for the skywalk entry.</li><li>A warm layer for the sunset, which turns cool quickly by the sea.</li></ul><p>For the sea part of the day, see the <a href="/cabo-girao-boat-tour">boat trip under Cabo Girão</a>, or compare <a href="/experiences">both Chifbay trips side by side</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Do you need a car for the afternoon?</h3><p>It is easiest. Câmara de Lobos is about 15 minutes from Funchal, Cabo Girão a short drive uphill from there, and Ponta do Sol about 20 minutes further west. Taxis also work.</p><h3>How much does the Cabo Girão skywalk cost?</h3><p>In 2026 entry costs 5 EUR for visitors. Children up to 12 and Madeira residents go in free.</p><h3>Is the 2h30 or the 3h Day Trip better for this plan?</h3><p>Both fit. The 3h trip is back at 13:00 and adds Ponta do Sol from the sea, which pairs well with ending the day there.</p><h3>What if the boat trip is cancelled for weather?</h3><p>The skipper decides on the day. Rebook or take a full refund, and the afternoon on land still works.</p>

      <blockquote>Morning under the cliff, afternoon on top of it, sunset where the boat turned round.</blockquote>
    </article>
    <p class="pref-src" data-pref-source><span>Enjoying our Madeira guides?</span> <a href="https://www.google.com/preferences/source?q=chifbay.com" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" width="18" height="18" aria-hidden="true"><path fill="#4285F4" d="M23.5 12.3c0-.8-.1-1.6-.2-2.3H12v4.5h6.5a5.6 5.6 0 0 1-2.4 3.6v3h3.9c2.2-2.1 3.5-5.1 3.5-8.8z"/><path fill="#34A853" d="M12 24c3.2 0 6-1.1 7.9-2.9l-3.9-3c-1.1.7-2.4 1.2-4 1.2-3.1 0-5.7-2.1-6.6-4.9h-4v3.1A12 12 0 0 0 12 24z"/><path fill="#FBBC05" d="M5.4 14.4a7.2 7.2 0 0 1 0-4.7V6.6h-4a12 12 0 0 0 0 10.8l4-3z"/><path fill="#EA4335" d="M12 4.8c1.7 0 3.3.6 4.6 1.8l3.4-3.4A12 12 0 0 0 1.4 6.6l4 3.1C6.3 6.9 8.9 4.8 12 4.8z"/></svg>Add Chifbay as a preferred source on Google</a></p>

